WEBVTT

00:02:30.461 --> 00:02:34.141
"Ping-pong" sounds
like a cousin of "sing-song,"

00:02:34.165 --> 00:02:36.263
like something Eastern,

00:02:36.287 --> 00:02:41.503
but actually, it's believed
that it was invented by high-class Brits

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:43.297
during Victorian times,

00:02:43.321 --> 00:02:48.391
who started hitting wine corks
over walls of books after dinner.

00:02:48.415 --> 00:02:49.464
(Laughter)

00:02:49.488 --> 00:02:50.670
No exaggeration.

00:02:50.694 --> 00:02:51.764
(Laughter)

00:02:51.788 --> 00:02:53.750
And by the end of World War I,

00:02:53.774 --> 00:02:59.471
the sport was dominated by players
from the former Austro-Hungarian Empire:

00:02:59.495 --> 00:03:02.531
eight out of nine
early world championships